From: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 17:00:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: pcrypt - Fix handling of MAY_BACKLOG requests
Git-commit: 915b692e6cb723aac658c25eb82c58fd81235110
Patch-mainline: v7.1-rc1
References: CVE-2026-43493 bsc#1265627

MAY_BACKLOG requests can return EBUSY.  Handle them by checking
for that value and filtering out EINPROGRESS notifications.

Reported-by: Yiming Qian <yimingqian591@gmail.com>
Fixes: 5a1436beec57 ("crypto: pcrypt - call the complete function on error")
Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
---
 crypto/pcrypt.c |    7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/crypto/pcrypt.c
+++ b/crypto/pcrypt.c
@@ -129,6 +129,9 @@ static void pcrypt_aead_done(struct cryp
 	struct pcrypt_request *preq = aead_request_ctx(req);
 	struct padata_priv *padata = pcrypt_request_padata(preq);
 
+	if (err == -EINPROGRESS)
+		return;
+
 	padata->info = err;
 
 	padata_do_serial(padata);
@@ -141,7 +144,7 @@ static void pcrypt_aead_enc(struct padat
 
 	padata->info = crypto_aead_encrypt(req);
 
-	if (padata->info == -EINPROGRESS)
+	if (padata->info == -EINPROGRESS || padata->info == -EBUSY)
 		return;
 
 	padata_do_serial(padata);
@@ -187,7 +190,7 @@ static void pcrypt_aead_dec(struct padat
 
 	padata->info = crypto_aead_decrypt(req);
 
-	if (padata->info == -EINPROGRESS)
+	if (padata->info == -EINPROGRESS || padata->info == -EBUSY)
 		return;
 
 	padata_do_serial(padata);
